@startuml
title sd CustomerIntake - Customer Portal Submission & Clarification\nMB-SEQ-0.2 compatibility candidate, 2026-09-14
mainframe sd - independent interaction named in page title
footer Independent interaction definitions; no cross-frame trace continuation
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF4F8
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #27465B
skinparam ArrowColor #27465B
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF5D9
autonumber
actor "End Customer" as C
boundary "Customer Portal UI\n(Next.js / B)" as UI
control "Domain Service & API\n(Authoritative / A)" as DS
entity "Authoritative Store" as DB
control "Coordinator Agent\n(A's AI Intake Role)" as CA
boundary "Notification Port\n(Mock Provider)" as NP

note over UI, DB
  All HTTP calls require a verified Bearer session and role/resource access.
  Every POST uses a scoped Idempotency-Key and validated payload.
  Domain alone commits business state; diagrams specify planned behavior.
  This CustomerIntake interaction invokes definition 2 only through the fresh-branch refs.
  Definition 2 is separate; its lifelines/messages do not continue this trace.
end note
== 1. Optional Evidence Staging ==
C -> UI : Select optional evidence; pass local format checks
UI -> DS : POST /v1/evidence\n(Bearer, Idempotency-Key, multipart file/description)
DS -> DS : Authenticate CUSTOMER; validate actual format/size\nand scoped upload replay before any new write
DS -> DB : Fresh accepted upload: persist owner-private\nSTAGED EvidenceAttachment and receipt
DS --> UI : 201 EvidenceAttachment (server evidence_id)
note over UI, DB
  JPEG/PNG/PDF <= 10 MiB each; <= 10 references per create/clarification.
  Only successfully staged IDs may be submitted; staging grants no case mutation.
  Upload replay uses the same receipt/retention rules below.
end note
== 2. UC-01 Case Creation ==
C -> UI : Submit original statement and optional fields
UI -> DS : POST /v1/cases (Bearer, Idempotency-Key)\nCreateCaseRequest(original_message, optional order_reference,\nrequested_outcome and evidence_ids)
DS -> DS : Authenticate/validate; find accepted record in\nprincipal + method/route + target + key scope
DS -> DB : Read acceptance fingerprint and receipt availability
alt Accepted key, different canonical request
  DS --> UI : 409 IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT; no new work
else Accepted key, identical request, receipt wholly readable
  DS --> UI : Original 201 CustomerCaseView receipt; no new work
  UI -> DS : GET /v1/cases/{case_id} (Bearer)
  DS --> UI : Authorised current CustomerCaseView
else Accepted key, identical request, receipt content removed
  DS --> UI : 409 INVALID_STATE, retryable=false\nPreviously accepted; original receipt unavailable
  UI -> UI : Do not change key or resubmit intent;\nread authorised current case/history when accessible
else Fresh valid submission
  DS -> DB : Atomic admission: bind available owned STAGED IDs;\ncreate ReturnCase SUBMITTED, ORIGINAL CustomerStatement,\ncase-owned IntakeSession SUBMITTED, intake work and receipt
  DS --> UI : 201 CustomerCaseView (accepted commit)
  UI --> C : Show accepted submission; load current progress
  ref over DS, NP : ProcessAcceptedIntake (definition 2; newly accepted initial work)
end
note over UI, DS
  Unknown response: recover with the same key and original request.
  Replayed receipt is historical, never asserted to be the current view.
  Auth/schema/admission failures return a safe correlated ErrorEnvelope.
end note
UI -> DS : GET /v1/cases/{case_id} (Bearer; own case)
DS --> UI : Current CustomerCaseView with case_version,\nclarification when present and collection_windows
UI --> C : Render server-confirmed status and safe customer fields
== 4. UC-01E Repeatable Clarification ==
loop While current case is AWAITING_INFORMATION and customer chooses to answer
  C -> UI : Answer current targeted questions and/or provide evidence
  opt New evidence selected
    ref over UI, DB : Stage new files with flow 1; use returned evidence IDs
  end
  UI -> DS : POST /v1/cases/{case_id}/clarifications (Bearer, Idempotency-Key)\nClarificationRequest(expected_case_version=current.case_version,\nquestion_set_id=current.clarification.question_set_id, answers, evidence_ids)
  DS -> DS : Authenticate owner and validate; resolve accepted\nreplay before checking a new intent against current state
  alt Accepted replay or request rejected
    DS --> UI : Original readable 202 receipt or safe ErrorEnvelope\n(removed receipt -> 409 INVALID_STATE; payload mismatch -> 409 IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT)
    UI -> UI : No new input/analysis; recover as flow 2;\non stale/conflicting admission reload before confirming a new intent
  else Fresh request with current owner/state/question set/version
    DS -> DB : Atomically recheck AWAITING_INFORMATION, expected_case_version,\nquestion_set_id and answer references; bind owned available STAGED IDs;\nappend CLARIFICATION statements; advance case/input versions;\ninvalidate stale derived authority; IntakeSession CLARIFICATION_RECEIVED;\npersist intake work and receipt
    DS --> UI : 202 CustomerCaseView (accepted input; not completed case)
    ref over DS, NP : ProcessAcceptedIntake (definition 2; newly accepted clarification work)
  end
  UI -> DS : GET /v1/cases/{case_id} (Bearer; own case)
  DS --> UI : Current CustomerCaseView; remaining clarification if still incomplete
  UI --> C : Show remaining relevant questions or confirmed progress
end
opt Customer leaves the page or does not respond
  C -> UI : Close/pause local IntakeViewSession
  note over C, DB
    No cancellation/withdrawal HTTP request or server transition occurs.
    No three-round escalation or seven-day archive policy is approved here.
    Reopening reads the current authorised case; F.07 retention still applies.
  end note
end

newpage sd ProcessAcceptedIntake - Independent Interaction Definition\nMB-SEQ-0.2; invoked only by fresh-work refs in sd CustomerIntake
autonumber 1
note over DS, NP
  Independent interaction definition; fresh lifelines, not continuation of definition 1.
  Precondition: a fresh input/work/receipt commit was accepted in sd CustomerIntake.
  Replayed or rejected requests have no invocation and no path to these messages.
end note
== 3. Common Accepted Intake Processing (Initial or Clarification Input) ==
DS -> DB : Load selected work/current input; IntakeSession EVALUATING
DS -> CA : Accepted Coordinator input with exact case/input,\noriginal statement ID and authorised available source references
CA --> DS : CoordinatorResult or actual technical error
DS -> DS : Validate schema and current case/input/work bindings;\ndiscard obsolete result; bounded recovery for actual errors
alt Valid current result: mandatory facts sufficient
  DS -> DB : Persist facts; ReturnCase UNDER_INVESTIGATION;\nIntakeSession COMPLETE; hand off to UC-02
else Valid current result: missing/ambiguous facts
  DS -> DB : Atomically persist facts and current ClarificationSet;\nReturnCase AWAITING_INFORMATION; IntakeSession AWAITING_CLARIFICATION;\nadvance internal clarification_round on newly issued question set
  DS -> NP : After commit, notify customer of targeted questions
  NP --> DS : Record observed delivery outcome separately
else Current processing failed; bounded recovery exhausted
  DS -> DB : Persist actual ProcessingFailure (COORDINATOR, exact input);\nReturnCase ESCALATED under existing target guards;\nIntakeSession ESCALATED_FAILURE
  note over DS, DB
    No current proposal: exactly one current ProcessingFailure or OrderLookupBlock.
    This branch uses a real failure, never a missing-facts/round-limit substitute.
    Preserve any existing proposal/history; Founder uses the applicable exact target.
    No automatic MANUAL_HANDLING, approval or operation is created.
  end note
end
legend bottom
  Original B delivery 92cd717; A/AI-assisted compatibility revision; B acceptance pending.
  AH-01 -> UC-01 / UC-01E -> M-B.03 (Criterion C9); no implemented API/DB claim.
  CustomerStatement uses statement_id/kind/raw_text, not an invented version field.
  CustomerCaseView.clarification and collection_windows follow F.01; no internal review leakage.
endlegend
@enduml
